# 0001 · Pre-production: steps with nothing to act on are inactive

- Status: accepted
- Date: @@TODAY@@
- Guide version: @@GUIDE_VERSION@@
- Rules concerned: DEL-CI-001

## Context

DEL-CI-001 makes every CI step mandatory and allows disabling one only through
an ADR. A new repository has steps with nothing to act on yet.

## Decision

A step that has nothing to act on prints `inactive: <reason>` and passes:

| Step | Inactive while |
|---|---|
| `api-diff` | there is no release tag yet, or the core sdk has no contract exporter yet |
| `test-e2e` | the app has no end-to-end spec yet |

Every other step always runs. A step that does not apply to the repository at
all (the frontend steps of an app without a frontend) prints
`not applicable` instead.

## Consequences

- CI is green from the first commit while still running everything that can run.
- Each inactive step activates by itself when its precondition appears.
- `api-diff` fails once the exporter exists, until the recipe uses it: the gap
  cannot stay unnoticed.

## Review

Remove this ADR, and the inactive branches, once both steps are active.
